          "short": "Intercepts: $(-3\\sqrt3,0)$, $(0,0)$ and $(3\\sqrt3,0)$. Local minimum: $(-3,-54)$. Local maximum: $(3,54)$. Point of inflection: $(0,0)$.",
          "worked": "Find the intercepts:\n$$\\begin{align*}27x-x^3&=0\\\\x(27-x^2)&=0\\\\x&=0,\\ \\pm3\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$\nPlot the intercepts, the local minimum $(-3,-54)$, the local maximum $(3,54)$ and the point of inflection $(0,0)$. The curve is increasing for $-3<x<3$ and decreasing for $x<-3$ and $x>3$. It is concave up for $x<0$ and concave down for $x>0$. As $x\\to-\\infty$, $y\\to\\infty$; as $x\\to\\infty$, $y\\to-\\infty$. Join these features with a smooth cubic curve having rotational symmetry about the origin.",
